Real predictor outputs for the same complex, made on 2026-09-27 to test that Proteus reads each
predictor's files as written: chain A MKTAYIAKQRQISFVKSHFSRQLEERLGLS with a phosphoserine (SEP)
at position 14, chain B ubiquitin 1-56 (MQIFVKTLTGKTITLEVEPSDTIENVKAKIQDKEGIPPDQQRLIFAGKQLEDGRTL),
and one ATP. No MSA, one sample. Structures are gzipped; confidence files are cut to the keys
Proteus reads, values unchanged.

boltz2/    Boltz 2.2.1 (ghcr.io/jwohlwend/boltz), msa: empty, one sample, mmCIF. 117 tokens: the SEP
           is one token (Boltz-2's convention). ipSAE 0.253391 / 0.063016 and LIS 0.3937 are what
           DunbrackLab ipsae.py (6174cf9) gives on this model with the ATP removed, the SEP read as
           SER and the PAE cut to its first 86 rows; on the files as they are it reports
           0.619150 / 0.264946 (DunbrackLab/IPSAE#28). Boltz is MIT.

protenix/  Protenix 2.0.0, model protenix_mini_default_v0.5.0, seed 101, --need_atom_confidence.
           126 tokens: the SEP is one token per heavy atom (AlphaFold 3's convention).
           The expected values in tests/interface.rs were computed by hand from Protenix's own
           atom_to_token_idx map, independently of Proteus. Protenix is Apache-2.0.

openfold3_json/  OpenFold3 0.5.0 (OpenBind-0 parameters, of3-ob-2025-06-30-174k), seed 2746317213,
openfold3_npz/   --use_msa_server=False; the second run with full_confidence_output_format: npz
                 (float16, OpenFold3's default dtype for it). ATP was given as SMILES and is written
                 as LIG0. 126 tokens: AlphaFold 3's convention; Boltz-2's would give 117. Confidence
                 files are cut to `pae`. Expected values were computed by hand from the model and
                 the matrix with that token rule, independently of Proteus. OpenFold3 is Apache-2.0.
